        "procedure": "Method A: To a toluene solution (5 mL) of 1 (245 mg, 0.2 mmol) was added ArOH (Ar = C6H2tBu2-2,6-Me-4) (44 mg, 0.2 mmol) in 5 mL toluene. Stirred at room temperature 8 h. Volume reduction gave green precipitates, recrystallized from hot toluene (65 mg, 23% based on Sm). Phenylacetylene likewise gave 4. Method B (high-yield): a toluene solution (5 mL) of 1 (245 mg, 0.2 mmol) was added to a toluene solution (5 mL) of 5 (217 mg, 0.2 mmol) at room temperature. After stirring 2 h, solvent was removed, residue washed with hexane and dried (370 mg, 85%). Reaction of 1 (245 mg, 0.2 mmol) with 8 (188 mg, 0.1 mmol) also gave 4 (355 mg, 82%). Dark green blocks for X-ray from concentrated hot toluene.",
